  "id": "Compound::DB00511 - Gene::483",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset suggests a potential relationship between Acetyldigitoxin and Atp1b3, mediated through the protein Fxyd2. Acetyldigitoxin is reported to bind to Fxyd2, which is involved in the sodium-potassium-exchanging Atpase Complex and the potassium-transporting Atpase Activity. These activities are ultimately associated with Atp1b3, indicating a pathway where Acetyldigitoxin may influence the function of Atp1b3 through Fxyd2. The scores from the three paths, ranging from 0.7457 to 0.758, suggest a consistent and significant interaction, though the exact nature of the binding and its functional impact on Atp1b3 remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Acetyldigitoxin and Atp1b3, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the role of Fxyd2 in this relationship.",
